2. Line 12272: For BOOL/NULL cases, it converts to Int32 but doesn't free the original `val`, which could leak memory.

3. Line 12294: When handling strings, if `JS_ToCStringLen` fails, it returns JS_EXCEPTION but doesn't free `val`, leaking memory.

